CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ move assignment template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
is not accessible
--
The preference for a non-template candidate was applied before the
comparison of reference bindings, so the deleted copy assignment beat a
move assignment operator template for an rvalue argument.  The MSVC STL's
unique_ptr declares its move assignment as a template
(cpp11_unique_ptr_move on VS 2022).
